{"availability":"available","full":"lblankl/SWE-MiniSandbox","name":"SWE-MiniSandbox","description":"Container-free RL framework for training software engineering agents","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":82,"forks":6,"created":"2025-12-30T18:19:58Z","updated":"2026-06-24T10:03:22Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lblankl.github.io/SWE-MiniSandbox/","topics":["agent","agent-based-framework","ai","llm","reinforcement-learning","swe-agent"],"demo":"https://lblankl.github.io/SWE-MiniSandbox/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.851Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.851Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.851Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.851Z","stars":82,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SWE-MiniSandbox is a lightweight, container-free framework for isolating batched SWE agent interactions and computing execution-based rewards. It also supports multi-node, on-policy reinforcement learning training without relying on Kubernetes or other container orchestration systems.","The framework relies on Linux namespaces, chroot, and bind mounts to create secure and efficient environments where SWE agents can interact with the system while remaining isolated from one another.","Python environments are isolated using venv, ensuring that each agent has its own dependencies without interference. These venvs are managed using different versions of Conda, providing flexibility in the software stack available to each agent."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lblankl/SWE-MiniSandbox/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"c137fd4248f7fb9f798ba64929e75b3186b83a82906a7088ec571d2db61d1773","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:18.009Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:18.009Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SWE-MiniSandbox is a lightweight, container-free framework for isolating batched SWE agent interactions and computing exe